  "//": "Stone fruit — peach, nectarine, sweet cherry, apricot. Agronomic entries are scoped by deviceNamePattern to placeholders (%peach% (also nectarines), %cherry%, %apricot%) — rename devices to match or replace the pattern with deviceProfiles before trusting an alert. Thresholds are the published extension figures cited in each entry; they are starting points, not calibrations.",
  "//months": "activeMonths are Central Valley timing: bloom February–March.",
  "//enabled": "Enabled: checks whose threshold is a published figure the sensor measures directly — air, leaf and soil temperature, humidity, durations, rates, pH. Disabled: checks whose threshold depends on this soil or this probe (volumetric moisture, EC, N, the 'wet' cut-off of a leaf-wetness sensor) or that need the forecast block — each says what to set before enabling it.",
