      "//": "ROOT-ZONE SALINITY — peach: Maas–Hoffman threshold ECe 1.7 dS/m, above which yield declines. DISABLED until converted to what the probe reads. Maas–Hoffman thresholds are saturated-paste ECe. A soil probe reports bulk EC (or pore EC), which is not ECe: FAO 29 gives soil-water EC ≈ 2 × ECe at field capacity, and bulk EC is lower than pore EC and moves with water content. Convert before enabling — take a saturated-paste lab sample beside the probe and scale this threshold by the probe/ECe ratio. Source: FAO Irrigation and Drainage Paper 29, ch. 2 and Annex 1 (Maas & Grattan 1999), https://www.fao.org/4/t0234e/t0234e02.htm , https://www.fao.org/4/y4263e/y4263e0e.htm",
      "rule": "measurement-threshold",
      "as": "peach-salinity-high",
      "enabled": false,
      "params": {
        "paths": ["soil.ec"],
        "min": null,
        "max": 1.7,
        "unit": " dS/m",
        "clearMargin": 0.17,
        "sustainMinutes": 1440,
        "lookbackHours": 48,
        "deviceNamePattern": "%peach%"
      }
    },
